# Campus Events API: test requests
# Use with the "REST Client" extension in VS Code: click "Send Request" under each ###.
# The backend must be running on port 4000. Restart it first for clean seed data.
# Run A2 (register) and A7 (login) before any request that needs a token.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api
@email = almaz@example.et
@password = Password123!

# ===================== AUTH =====================

### A1. Invalid email (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "not-an-email", "password": "{{password}}" }

### A2. Register a new user (expect 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### A3. Same email again (expect 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### A4. Short password (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "new@example.et", "password": "123" }

### A5. Extra role field (expect 400, needs forbidNonWhitelisted: true)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "new@example.et", "password": "{{password}}", "roles": ["ADMIN"] }

### A6. Wrong password (expect 401, "Invalid credentials")
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "WrongPassword123!" }

### A6b. Unknown email (expect the same 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nobody@example.et", "password": "{{password}}" }

### A7. Login (expect 201 with accessToken and refreshToken)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### A8. Current user without a token (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### A9. Current user with a valid token (expect 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### A10. Tampered token (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}x

# ===================== EVENTS: PUBLIC READS =====================

### 1. Get all events (expect 200, default limit 5)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events

### 2. Filter by category (expect 200, only technology events)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?category=technology

### 3. Filter by publication status (expect 200, only published events)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?isPublished=true

### 4. Sort and paginate (expect 200, page 2 of the date-sorted list)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?sortBy=eventDate&order=asc&page=2&limit=2

### 5. Get upcoming events (expect 200, events dated today or later)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/upcoming

### 6. Get an existing event (expect 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/evt-101

### 7. Missing event (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/not-real

### 8. Sessions for an event (expect 200, array)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/evt-101/sessions

### 9. Session under its event (expect 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/evt-101/sessions/ses-201

# ===================== CREATE EVENT =====================

### 10. Create a valid event with a token (expect 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "title": "Intro to Cloud Computing",
  "description": "A beginner-friendly campus workshop.",
  "location": "Engineering Block, Room 2",
  "eventDate": "2026-12-04T09:00:00.000Z",
  "category": "technology",
  "isPublished": true
}

### 11. Missing title, with a token (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "description": "A beginner-friendly campus workshop.",
  "location": "Engineering Block, Room 2",
  "eventDate": "2026-12-04T09:00:00.000Z",
  "category": "technology",
  "isPublished": true
}

### 11b. Create without a token (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Test",
  "description": "x",
  "location": "y",
  "eventDate": "2026-12-04T09:00:00.000Z",
  "category": "technology",
  "isPublished": true
}

# ===================== EXTRA CHECKS =====================

### 12. Session that belongs to a different event (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/evt-101/sessions/ses-203

### 13. Event with no sessions (expect 200, empty array)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/evt-102/sessions

### 14. Unsupported sort field (expect 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?sortBy=price

### 15. Invalid page number (expect 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?page=0

### 16. Page past the end (expect 200, empty items)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?page=99

### 17. Location filter, partial match (expect 200, locations containing "main")
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?location=main

# ===================== REFRESH AND LOGOUT (run in order) =====================

### R1. Refresh (expect 201, new token pair)
# @name refresh
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.refreshToken}}" }

### R2. Reuse the old refresh token (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.refreshToken}}" }

### R3. Logout (expect 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh.response.body.accessToken}}

### R4. Refresh after logout (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refresh.response.body.refreshToken}}" }